# What a gateway is, carried across a firmware upgrade.
#
# sysupgrade keeps /etc/config/* and whatever is listed in keep.d, and nothing
# else. Before this file existed that meant /etc/config/parkeze survived — the
# UCI that says "adopted" — while everything that makes the adoption usable was
# thrown away. An upgraded gateway believed it was adopted and could not prove
# who it was: the claim secret was gone, so its reports were refused.
#
# The WireGuard keypair is kept for the same reason: the hub knows this
# gateway by its public key, so a new key after every upgrade would mean
# re-enrolling, and a tunnel that is down until it does.
#
# board.conf is deliberately NOT here. It describes the image, and has to come
# from the new one or the gateway would report the old version forever.
/etc/parkeze/claim/
/etc/parkeze/console/
/etc/parkeze/wireguard/
/etc/parkeze/recovery.pub
